# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BACKUPS — one rule, one location. (Established 2026-08-08.)
#
# Every safety copy required by Sacred Rule #1 is made with
# `engineering/tools/backup-file.sh <path>` and lands in .backups/, mirroring the file's
# repo-relative path with a timestamp appended. That keeps backups OUT of the
# working tree, so they can never be picked up by a grep, glob, find, audit
# script, or source-selection step — the failure that once had backup copies
# of the DeSilva opus-masters mistaken for the live source.
#
# This single line replaced fifteen accumulated rules (eight naming shapes,
# three of them naming individual files by hand). Do not add per-file backup
# rules here; use the script and this rule covers it.
/.backups/

# Defensive net for backups made by *other* tools (editors, `sed -i.bak`,
# `patch`, merge conflicts) that don't route through the script.
*.bak
*.bak[0-9]
*.backup
*.backup.*
*.backup-*
*.orig
*.rej

# Legacy backup directories (pre-2026-08-08; contents relocated to .backups/)
**/backups/
backups/

# Roving central-skills staging area (carried between repos; not project-versioned)
central-skills-staging/

# Parallel ingestion-wave staging (transient; map agents stage here, ingest-wrap-reduce promotes + tears down)
engineering/ingestion/_staging/

# Parallel boundary-determination staging (transient; mine-and-delineate map agents stage here, the reduce promotes + tears down)
engineering/document-production/_mine-staging/

# Reference tools staged into the container but never versioned (e.g. flexspin binary)
REF-TOOLS-NO-COMMIT/

